-- title:
--   Strong approximation at a split place for indefinite quaternion orders
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, let $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and assume $0<a$ or $0<b$, and that every nonzero element of $B$ is a unit. Let $O\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated. Let $w$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, and assume $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ contains a nonzero non-unit. Then there is $s\in B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ with $s\neq 1$ and $s\neq -1$ such that: (i) for every ring isomorphism $\varphi\colon B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w\to\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(\text{the coordinatewise image of }z)$ for all $z\in B$, $r\in\mathbb{Q}_w$, one has $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi(s))=1$, where $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_0^2-ax_1^2-bx_2^2+abx_3^2$; and (ii) for every nonzero $M\in\mathbb{N}$ there is $\beta\in B$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\beta)=1$ such that for each height-one prime $w'\neq w$ there is $z$ in the additive subgroup of $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_{w'}$ generated by the elements $y\otimes c$ with $y\in O$ and $c$ in the valuation ring, with $\beta\otimes 1=1+M\cdot z$, and likewise some such $z$ at $w$ with $\beta\otimes 1=s+M\cdot z$.
--
--   This is the local input to strong approximation for the norm-one group of an indefinite quaternion division algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$: at a finite place where the algebra splits one produces a non-central local element of reduced norm one that is approximated, to any prescribed congruence level, by global elements of reduced norm one congruent to $1$ at all other finite places. It is used in the construction of norm-one elements with prescribed idelic behaviour and in the results on maximal orders that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_ne_neg_one_forall_exists_nrd_eq_one_tmul_eq_add_smul_of_forall_isUnit.lean

